## Commands

| Command | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `graph-agents-cli playground` | Run the app with reload and open the dev chat page |
| `graph-agents-cli run "prompt"` | One-shot chat (`--mode a2a` for the A2A path, `--url` for a deployed agent) |
| `uv run pytest` | Unit and integration tests (fake model, in-memory checkpointer) |
| `graph-agents-cli eval run` | Generate traces and grade them against the gate |
| `graph-agents-cli lint` | ruff plus the API-policy check of every tool |
| `graph-agents-cli api show` / `api check` | The outbound API policy and each tool's declared calls / the policy check alone |
| `graph-agents-cli build` | Build the container image from the runtime's Dockerfile |
| `graph-agents-cli deploy --env <env>` | Deploy (direct modes) or open the desired-state PR (argocd) |
| `graph-agents-cli secrets apply --env <env>` | Create or update the environment's app Secret from `.env.<env>` |
| `graph-agents-cli secrets status --env <env>` | Which keys the Secret holds (never values); exit 1 on a missing required key |
| `graph-agents-cli infra check --env <env>` | Read-only report of cluster and GitHub prerequisites |

## Rules

- **Spec before code** unless the governing process says otherwise (see above).
- **Change only what was asked.** Preserve surrounding code, comments, config values and formatting.
- **Never change the model** (`MODEL_PROVIDER`, `MODEL_NAME`) unless explicitly asked.
  A model 404 means the name is wrong for the provider or the endpoint; fix the
  configuration in `.env`, not `{{cookiecutter.agent_directory}}/agent.py`.
- **Human approval before deploy.** Never run `graph-agents-cli deploy` without the user's explicit go-ahead,
  and never pass `--yes` (accepting the kubeconfig's current context) or `--rotate-api-key` on your own.
- **Run Python through uv**: `uv run python script.py`, after `uv sync`.
- **Three strikes.** The same error three times means fix the cause, not retry.
- **Tools declare their API calls.** Add an `API_CALLS` entry (`api`, `method`,
  `operation_id` and/or `path`) for every external API call a tool makes;
  `graph-agents-cli lint` refuses undeclared or disallowed calls. Never bypass
  `api_client.py` with a raw HTTP client.
- **Change `api-policy.yaml` only when the user asks**, with `graph-agents-cli api`
  (`add`, `access`, `allow`, `deny`, `revoke`, `limits`, `remove`; show the user the
  printed diff, use `--dry-run` first). The policy is a security boundary: never
  widen access (more methods or operations, a lifted denial, a raised limit) on your
  own, and never add an `approval` key (not supported yet). When a tool needs a call
  the policy refuses, `lint` prints the command that would allow it: propose it,
  do not run it unasked. Widening goes through a pull request reviewed by the code owners.
- **Never edit `graph-agents-cli-manifest.yaml` or `values-prod.yaml`** unless the
  user asks: production desired state changes only through a pull request reviewed
  by the code owners.
- **Do not export prompts or user data** to a hosted tracing destination unless
  the user has decided so (`TRACING_ENABLED`, `TRACE_CAPTURE=full`).
- **Never log credentials, prompts or tool arguments**, and keep secrets out of
  `Principal.attributes` except under `attributes["credentials"]`.
- **Respect the guardrails** (`RUN_TIMEOUT_S`, `RECURSION_LIMIT`, the one-run-per-thread 409):
  fix a tool or graph that hits them instead of raising the limits, unless the user asks.
